From 9a61a393dec17696dc7d2cf4094e2ce13edcf7b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MotherSphere <mothersphere.colony@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 14:29:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(Lua): don't block loading threads on
 m_thread_actions_mutex in the StaticConstructObject hook

script_hook holds m_thread_actions_mutex while the Lua callback of a
RegisterHook on a Blueprint function runs. When that callback calls
LoadAsset, the game thread waits for the package. The async loading
thread constructs the objects of that package. The StaticConstructObject
post-callback made it wait for m_thread_actions_mutex, which the game
thread does not release while it waits for the load. Both threads stop
for good. The freeze goes away with -NoAsyncLoadingThread.

The two NotifyOnNewObject containers get their own mutex,
m_new_object_callbacks_mutex. Threads other than the game thread take
only this lock in the hook to read the callbacks and queue matches for
the game thread. The game thread still takes m_thread_actions_mutex in
the hook as before. Every access to the two containers takes the new
lock: registration, the hook, the game-thread drain, mod uninstall and
the reset in reinstall_mods. It is a leaf lock. No Lua function runs
while it is held. The game-thread branch copies each callback before it
calls Lua, so a NotifyOnNewObject call from Lua cannot reallocate the
vector under it.
---
Stellar Blade Online: tools/ue4ss_build.py applies this patch with git am
on UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS tag v4.0.0 (commit 30afe5ff) to build the UE4SS.dll
of SBO's UE4SS package. Issue: https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/issues/1504

 UE4SS/include/Mod/LuaMod.hpp |  4 ++
 UE4SS/src/Mod/LuaMod.cpp     | 75 ++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 UE4SS/src/UE4SSProgram.cpp   |  5 ++-
 3 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/UE4SS/include/Mod/LuaMod.hpp b/UE4SS/include/Mod/LuaMod.hpp
index 4c494a96..e9cc1d24 100644
--- a/UE4SS/include/Mod/LuaMod.hpp
+++ b/UE4SS/include/Mod/LuaMod.hpp
@@ -162,6 +162,10 @@ namespace RC
         static inline std::vector<DelayedGameThreadAction> m_pending_delayed_game_thread_actions{};
         // Pending NotifyOnNewObject callbacks to be processed on game thread
         static inline std::vector<PendingNotifyOnNewObjectCallback> m_pending_notify_on_new_object_callbacks{};
+        // Guards m_static_construct_object_lua_callbacks and m_pending_notify_on_new_object_callbacks, and nothing else.
+        // Loading threads take only this lock in the StaticConstructObject hook. They must not wait for m_thread_actions_mutex: the game thread holds it
+        // while Lua runs, and Lua can wait for those threads (LoadAsset). Leaf lock: take no other lock and call no Lua function while holding it.
+        static inline std::mutex m_new_object_callbacks_mutex{};
         // Flag to track if we're currently iterating over action vectors
         static inline bool m_is_processing_actions{};
         static inline GameThreadExecutionMethod m_default_game_thread_method{GameThreadExecutionMethod::EngineTick};
diff --git a/UE4SS/src/Mod/LuaMod.cpp b/UE4SS/src/Mod/LuaMod.cpp
index 61f5b987..75a5e1ce 100644
--- a/UE4SS/src/Mod/LuaMod.cpp
+++ b/UE4SS/src/Mod/LuaMod.cpp
@@ -2353,14 +2353,17 @@ Overloads:
                 class_outer_fname = Unreal::FName(name_parts.front(), Unreal::FNAME_Add);
